  "notes": [
    "DRAFT: a skeleton from the world database export of map 189 (tools/dungeongen, spec tools/dungeongen/plans.json). The boss order is the usual clear order, the packs are the spawn clusters nearest each boss; walls, doors, stairs and events are unknown to it. Not mapped, not live-checked: do the GM-invisible mapping walk and correct the route before the first run (AUTO-IMPROVE step 0); dungeon_run refuses it without allow_draft.",
    "A wait_for on a door a lever or key opens needs timeout_s 60 (the default): a linked door can open 30 s after the use.",
    "One of four wings of map 189; the packs are the ones inside the wing's box.",
    "Duke Dreadmoore (61972) is a Turtle addition in the crypt level (z -3.7): script npc_duke_dreadmoore sets him to 20 % health on reset and yells on aggro and death; his crypt pack is needs_walk until the mapping walk",
    "Census 2026-10-23 (176 spawns in the box: 136 hostile trash 25-33 rank 1, 4 bosses, 16 Suffering Victim 6547 faction 68 Undercity civilian, 19 Rat 4075 critter, Vorrel Sengutz 3981 quest NPC): the plan pulled 6547 and 4075 as pack members, which a Horde party cannot fight (6547 is friendly, 4075 a critter); they are out of every group and the four pure groups (leg 0 groups 6 and 11, leg 2 groups 1 and 8) are gone. Fleers: 4283 4293 4306 6490 (EventAI 47); 4308 6426 6427 6488 6489 61971 do not flee. No healer; the casters are 4306 (Immolate 9276), 6488 (Cleave/Execute) and 6490 Azshir (Soul Siphon 9373, Call of the Grave 17831, Terrify): kill_first 6490. The undead trash cannot be Polymorphed: no_cc 4308 6426 6427 6488 6489 (the plan row has no column for it). No creature_groups; 6488 6489 6490 are rank 1 in the data (7 spawns each), pulled as crypt trash, no skip list.",
    "Vishas 3983 stands 4.5-6 yd from the Scryer 4293 of the Vishas leg's group 13 (inside his 20 yd detection): that group is gone and 4293 is boss.first. Scorn 14693 stands 9 yd from the 6426 of the Scorn leg's group 6: that group is gone and 6426 is boss.first. The Duke leg is last: its 36-spawn crypt pull (the Duke leg's group 2) is the plan's only needs_walk point and stays so (the mapping walk has not been done); the first three legs do not depend on it.",
    "Patrollers that are their own pull carry their creature_movement path as a patrol block (period estimated): the Scryer 27440 (leg 0 group 2), the Jailer 2583151 (leg 0 group 8), the Sentry 2583107 (leg 0 group 10, a beat between the crypt and the upper floor) and the Jailer 2583146 (the Duke leg's group 5). The wing has no door or lever object; the crypt is open."
  ],
